From: OpenWrt HA build <local>
Subject: [PATCH] owsync: harden the listener against unauthenticated clients

The sync port is reachable by every host that can route to the node.
Before this change any client could occupy all worker slots by staying
silent, make the server allocate up to MAX_MESSAGE_SIZE per connection
before the AES-GCM tag was checked, and hand json_tokener_parse() a buffer
without a NUL terminator.

- accept only connections from the addresses of the configured peers
  (standalone "owsync server" without peers keeps accepting everyone);
- socket send/receive timeouts of 30 seconds on every session;
- frames are capped at 64 KiB until the peer's HELLO has been validated,
  and empty frames are rejected;
- receive and decrypt buffers get a NUL terminator;
- a FileContent frame without path or data is malformed;
- the sync root boundary check requires a "/" after the prefix;
- fchmod() gets permission bits only, never setuid/setgid/sticky.

The two-node exchange is unchanged: both peers are configured on each
side, HELLO stays well below 64 KiB, and a healthy session finishes long
before a 30 second idle timeout.

diff -ruN owsync-1.2.0/owsync-1.2.0/include/net.h owsync-work/include/net.h
--- a/include/net.h	2026-02-11 23:25:14.000000000 +0200
+++ b/include/net.h	2026-10-22 20:51:11.263086231 +0300
@@ -47,10 +47,21 @@
     } payload;
 } message_t;
 
+/* Largest frame accepted before the peer's HELLO has been validated.
+ * A HELLO is a few hundred bytes; the full MAX_MESSAGE_SIZE is only
+ * granted once the peer proved it holds the key (or, in plain mode,
+ * spoke the protocol). */
+#define OWSYNC_PREAUTH_MAX_MESSAGE (64 * 1024)
+
+/* Socket send/receive timeout for sync sessions, in seconds. A peer that
+ * connects and goes silent must not hold a worker slot forever. */
+#define OWSYNC_IO_TIMEOUT_SEC 30
+
 /* TCP channel with optional encryption */
 typedef struct {
     int fd;                /* Socket file descriptor */
     bool is_encrypted;     /* True if using AES-256-GCM encryption */
+    uint32_t max_message;  /* Largest frame accepted on this channel right now */
 #ifdef ENABLE_ENCRYPTION
     security_context_t *security_ctx;  /* Encryption context (NULL if plain) */
 #endif
@@ -66,6 +77,12 @@
 int channel_send(channel_t *channel, message_t *msg);
 int channel_receive(channel_t *channel, message_t **out_msg);
 
+/* Restrict the server to connections from the configured peers.
+ * peers use the "addr[,source_addr]" format of the daemon configuration;
+ * every address a peer name resolves to is accepted. With count == 0 the
+ * server accepts any client (standalone "owsync server" mode). */
+void net_set_allowed_peers(char **peers, size_t count);
+
 /* Server mode: listen for incoming connections, spawn threads */
 int start_server(const char *host, const char *port, const char *key,
                  const char *root, const char *db_path, file_filter_t *filter,
